WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.096
In the year 907, Zhu Wen forced the young Emperor Ai of Tang to abdicate and founded the Later Liang dynasty at Kaifeng.

00:00:09.446 --> 00:00:13.646
The whole court held its breath.

00:00:13.996 --> 00:00:23.044
The young Emperor Ai presented the imperial jade seal, and the great Tang dynasty, which had lasted nearly three hundred years, came to an end.

00:00:23.394 --> 00:00:32.394
This jade seal symbolized the emperor's supreme power, and also the end of a glorious age.

00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:40.304
Zhu Wen had originally been a military governor holding great armies at the end of Tang; now, in a sudden turn, he became a founding emperor.

00:00:40.654 --> 00:00:43.726
He walked step by step up to the high platform.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:52.956
The Later Liang dynasty founded by Zhu Wen was the first dynasty to appear in the turbulent age of the Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms.

00:00:53.306 --> 00:01:02.570
From then on, the Central Plains entered the chaotic, turbulent period of the Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms, with rival heroes rising side by side.

